        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Join the Heart of Teton Valley: 18th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Kicks Off June 13</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/53730.webp" alt="Join the Heart of Teton Valley: 18th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Kicks Off June 13" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The&nbsp;<strong>Community Foundation of Teton Valley</strong>&nbsp;is proud to launch the&nbsp;<em>18th Annual Tin Cup Challenge</em>—a unique, community-wide fundraiser that brings together neighbors across the valley to support the organizations that make life in the Tetons vibrant, resilient, and connected.</p>

<p>From&nbsp;<strong>Friday, June 13, through Friday, July 25 at 5 PM</strong>, anyone can give to their favorite local nonprofits through a single, streamlined donation, which<strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;</strong><strong>partially</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>matched</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>by generous&nbsp;</strong><strong>businesses and individuals</strong>. This means your gift goes further to support the&nbsp;critical work, dedication, and impact of the nonprofits you care about most.</p>

<p><em>“Whether you’ve lived here for decades or just recently made Teton Valley your home, this is your opportunity to be part of something bigger,”</em> said Bonnie Self, Executive Director of the Community Foundation, <em>“The Tin Cup Challenge helps local nonprofits raise essential funds by offering a Matching Grant that incentivizes community engagement.”</em></p>

<h3><strong>why it Matters</strong></h3>

<p>In just 17 years, the Tin Cup Challenge has raised nearly&nbsp;<strong>$</strong><strong>27</strong><strong>&nbsp;million</strong>&nbsp;for Teton Valley nonprofits. These funds support vital programs in education, healthcare, social services, conservation, animal welfare, the arts, recreation, and more. In 2024 alone,&nbsp;<strong>$3.3 million</strong>&nbsp;was raised and has since been invested across the valley, fueling the daily work that keeps our community thriving year-round.</p>

<h3><strong>Join the Challenge</strong></h3>

<ol>
<li><strong>Give during the 6-week Giving Period</strong>&nbsp;(June 13–July 25):<ol><li>Donate by check (using the Tin Cup Donor Form)</li></ol><ol><li>Give online at&nbsp;<a href="http://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.org</a></li></ol>
<ol>
<li>Or contribute via stock, wire transfer, or donor-advised fund<br><strong>100% of your donation goes to the nonprofits you choose.</strong></li>
</ol>
</li>

<li><strong>Celebrate on Event Day</strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;<strong>Saturday, July 19 from 9 AM–Noon at Driggs City Park</strong><ol><li>Timed 5K /10K races, and Fun Run/Walk</li></ol><ol><li>Free community breakfast, entertainment, and activities</li></ol><ol><li>Nonprofit booths, information, and games</li></ol>
<ol>
<li>Complimentary T-shirts&nbsp;<em>(while supplies last)</em></li>
</ol>
</li>

<li>Become a Challenger ($1,500+) or Friend of the Match ($1+)<ol><li>Support the partial Match Grant for participating nonprofits</li></ol><ol><li>Fund&nbsp;Competitive Grants and&nbsp;Youth Philanthropy</li></ol>
<ol>
<li>Offer training opportunities for&nbsp;nonprofit board and staff members</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>

<h3><strong>New to the valley?</strong></h3>

<p>We invite you to explore the amazing work being done by over 60 local nonprofits! It’s a perfect way to get involved, meet your neighbors, and find where your passions align with community needs. Look for the&nbsp;<strong>Tin Cup brochure in your mailbox on June 13</strong>. Visit us online, at the&nbsp;<strong>Driggs Farmers Market</strong>&nbsp;each Friday through July 25, or at our office (189 North Main Street, Suite 112) to donate, pick up your free T-shirt, and register to run!</p>

<p>The Community Foundation would like to extend heartfelt gratitude to the Business and Community Challengers who have committed their support to this remarkable program.&nbsp;Together, we can ensure Teton Valley remains a place where generosity and community thrive.</p>

<p><strong>Give once. Impact many<a>.</a></strong><br><strong>Visit</strong>&nbsp;<a href="http://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.org</a>&nbsp;<strong>or call 208.354.0230 to learn more.</strong></p>
